implementationPlan.description:
Verification, run once. This command's fresh output is the complete_task evidence.

The path-contract tests import BOTH built dists, and a missing dist fails. Build them only in a scratch snapshot, never in the shared checkout (rail; mem:gotcha-path-contract-cross-impl-test):

`R=$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel) && S=$(mktemp -d) && git -C "$R" archive HEAD | tar -x -C "$S" && for f in scripts/moe-agent.sh scripts/tests/daemon-json-cap.test.mjs; do cp "$R/$f" "$S/$f" && cmp "$R/$f" "$S/$f" || exit 1; done && env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin" NO_COLOR=1 sh -c 'set -e; cd "$1/packages/moe-proxy"; npm ci --no-audit --no-fund --prefer-offline >/dev/null; npm run build >/dev/null; cd ../moe-daemon; npm ci --no-audit --no-fund --prefer-offline >/dev/null; npm run build >/dev/null; cd "$1"; bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh; node --test scripts/tests/daemon-json-cap.test.mjs; bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh' _ "$S"`

Expect:
- `# fail 0`;
- the dist test `path contract: moe-proxy and moe-daemon give every row its contract key` passes with the new rows;
- both `moe-agent.sh (python3)` path-contract tests pass;
- the identity rows pass;
- the parity check passes.

PS engines are skipped on Linux node. State that in the evidence. Windows CI runs them, and the step 1 pre-check found PS5.1 already agrees on every new row.

Afterwards, delete only that exact `$S` mktemp dir.

Error handling: a failed npm ci or build in the snapshot is an environment failure. Report it, and never retry in the shared checkout.
